<title>FINLAND: Finnish T-bill auction raises 1.51 bln markka.</title>
<headline>Finnish T-bill auction raises 1.51 bln markka.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the State Treasury Office's T-Bills auction on Tuesday compared to the September 17 auction  SUVK :</p>
<p>				This auction	Previous auction</p>
<p>				169-day T-bills   176-day T-bills</p>
<p> Av. yield, pct	   3.27 pct	    3.38 pct</p>
<p> Highest accepted	 3.29 pct	    3.38 pct</p>
<p> Lowest accepted	  3.26 pct	    3.38 pct</p>
<p> Amount, FIM million	  135		   170</p>
<p> Bids, million mk	     485		 1,123</p>
<p> Maturing date	    March 14, 1997    March 14, 1997</p>
<p>				263-day T-bills   277-day T-bills</p>
<p> Av. yield, pct	   3.41 pct	    3.50 pct</p>
<p> Highest accepted	 3.41 pct	    3.50 pct</p>
<p> Lowest accepted	  3.39 pct	    3.50 pct</p>
<p> Amount, FIM million	  550		   350</p>
<p> Bids, FIM million	    550		   950</p>
<p> Maturing date	    June 16, 1997     June 16, 1997</p>
<p>				This auction	 Previous auction</p>
<p>				354-day T-bills    361-day T-bills</p>
<p> Av. yield, pct	   3.51 pct	     3.60 pct</p>
<p> Highest accepted	 3.51 pct	     3.61 pct</p>
<p> Lowest accepted	  3.50 pct	     3.60 pct</p>
<p> Amount, million mk	   820		    962</p>
<p> Bids, million mk	   1,060		  2,132</p>
<p> Maturing date	    September 15, 1997 September 15, 1997</p>
<p>Total planned issue amount was 1.5 billion markka. After today's auction, the outstanding amount of treasury bills is 48,064 million markka, the STO said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
